  - blue-gray diagonal injection arrows from the time embedding baseline into every encoder, bottleneck, and decoder processing block
  - short blue-gray right-pointing arrows along the bottom baseline showing embedding flow
  - click-expanded self-attention overlay panel anchored near the 16×16 block, containing a 16×16 spatial grid, one highlighted query cell, attention-weight rays or heatmap over all positions, and a small contrasting plain residual-block mini-diagram

GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
Use an oblique architectural diagram with a wide horizontal layout about 16 world units wide and 5.5 units tall. Treat feature maps as thin cuboids with front faces in the drawing plane and depth receding up-right by about 0.28 world units. Approximate front-face heights by spatial resolution: 256→3.6 units, 128→1.8, 64→0.9, 32→0.48, 16→0.24, 8→0.16; keep tiny levels slightly enlarged for legibility. Width/thickness should suggest channel count rather than match it exactly: 3 channels very thin, 128 moderate, 256 wider, 512 widest/longest. Dominant colors: residual block front faces dark brown #7f3d22, side/top faces orange-copper #cf7d59, black outlines #000000, skip connections salmon #d57d5c, time embedding arrows blue-gray #4f6f80, attention legend arrow pale blue #9fc3d5, label text dark brown #854126. Input and output planes should use a gray/noise texture with slight color speckling. Timestep t ranges from 0 to 1000; show the current value numerically near the t node and encode it as a small sinusoidal embedding strip or color pulse traveling along each injection arrow. Self-attention overlay for 16×16 should show 256 spatial tokens, one highlighted query token, and attention weights distributed over all positions.

